.TH cc "" "Command"
.SH NAME
cc \- C compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcc [\fIoptions\fB] \fIfile ...\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
cc -- C compiler
Usage:	cc [ options ] file ...
Options:
	-B[str]		Use backup compiler versions
	-c		Compile only--no load
	-Dname[=value]	Tell cpp to define 'name' with 'value'
	-E		Run cpp only and send its output to stdout
	-f		Include floating point output routines in load
	-Iname		Tell cpp to look for include files in directory 'name'
	-K		Keep intermediate files
	-lname		Pass /lib/libname.a to linker
	-Mstr		Use alternative machine versions
	-O		Run peephole optimizer of C compiler
	-p		Compile and/or load for profiling
	-q[p01ab2s]	Quit after specified pass
	-S		Place C compiler assembler output in a '.s' file
	-t[p01ab2sdlrt]	Take specified compiler phases
	-Uname		Tell cpp to remove any initial definition of 'name'
	-V		Run verbosely, cf. -VSTAT
	-Vname		Toggle variant 'Vname'
Compiles files ending '.c'; assembles files ending in '.s';
passes other options and files to the linker 'ld'.
.HE
.B cc
is the C compiler driver.
It compiles each
.I file
that ends in
.BR .c ,
assembles each
.I file
that ends in
.BR .s ,
and passes all other options and files on to the linker
.BR ld .
.PP
.B cc
is itself a short shell script: it invokes the compiler controller
.B ccx
with a standard set of variants already enabled and hands it every
argument. Options are therefore interpreted by
.BR ccx .
.IP \fB\-B[\fIstr\fB]\fR
Use backup versions of the compiler passes.
.IP \fB\-c\fR
Compile only; do not load. Each source produces an object file and no
executable is linked.
.IP \fB\-D\fIname\fB[=\fIvalue\fB]\fR
Tell
.B cpp
to define
.I name
with the given
.IR value .
.IP \fB\-E\fR
Run
.B cpp
only and send its output to the standard output.
.IP \fB\-f\fR
Include the floating-point output routines in the load.
.IP \fB\-I\fIname\fR
Tell
.B cpp
to look for include files in directory
.IR name .
.IP \fB\-K\fR
Keep the intermediate files.
.IP \fB\-l\fIname\fR
Pass
.BI /lib/lib name .a
to the linker.
.IP \fB\-M\fIstr\fR
Use alternative machine versions.
.IP \fB\-O\fR
Run the peephole optimizer of the C compiler.
.IP \fB\-p\fR
Compile and/or load for profiling.
.IP \fB\-q[\fIp01ab2s\fB]\fR
Quit after the specified pass.
.IP \fB\-S\fR
Place the C compiler assembler output in a
.B .s
file.
.IP \fB\-t[\fIp01ab2sdlrt\fB]\fR
Take the specified compiler phases.
.IP \fB\-U\fIname\fR
Tell
.B cpp
to remove any initial definition of
.IR name .
.IP \fB\-V\fR
Run verbosely.
.IP \fB\-V\fIname\fR
Toggle the variant
.IR name .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
